{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And you stood beneath the mountain.</b> As it is written: ״ויתיצבו בתחתית ההר״ (they stationed themselves at the foot of the mountain)." "<b>And the mountain burned with fire to the heart of the heavens — darkness of cloud and fog.</b> And if you ask: this verse, its beginning contradicts its end — how so? A thing burning in fire, darkness does not rule there. Rather, both served together, and it goes on and explains how: ״וידבר אליכם מתוך האש״ — ״קול דבריםם that you were hearing, and ״תמונה אינכם רואים״ — by means of <b>darkness of cloud and fog</b> that was there, which did not give permission to gaze at the likeness of His glory." "<b>To the heart of the heavens.</b> In the middle, opposite the viewers."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:51:36.370566538Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}